\newlabel{tab:example_pairs}{{5.2}{59}{Second preference pair ($j = 2$) of the two dialogue contexts in Figure~\ref {fig:context_ranking}. The dialogue context (student error type) and the corresponding utility $u(m, e)$ are shown above each pair. Posterior and utility values are listed in the order \textit {Focus}, \textit {Generic}, \textit {Probing}, \textit {Telling}; the score is their inner product}{table.caption.6}{}}
